{"description": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "From back cover: Famous long before she was notorious, Cleopatra has gone down in history for all the wrong reasons; her supple personality and the drama of her circumstances have been lost. In a masterly return to the classical sources, Stacy Schiff boldly separates fact from fiction to rescue the magnetic queen whose death ushered in a new world order."}, "subtitle": "A Life", "title": "Cleopatra", "covers": [7083366, 6628614, 9097658], "subject_places": ["Egypt"], "subjects": ["Kings and rulers", "Queens", "Biography", "History", "Cleopatra, queen of egypt, -30 b.c.", "Egypt, kings and rulers", "Egypt, history, to 640 a.d.", "Egypt, biography", "nyt:paperback-nonfiction=2011-09-25", "New York Times bestseller", "New York Times reviewed", "nyt:paperback_nonfiction=2011-09-03", "Biografi", "Drottningar", "nyt:e-book-nonfiction=2011-02-13"], "subject_people": ["Cleopatra Queen of Egypt (d. 30 B.C)", "Julius Caesar", "Marcus Antonius, 83-30 B.C.", "Augustus, Emperor of Rome, 63 B.C.-14 A.D.", "Cleopatra Queen of Egypt (-30 B.C)"], "key": "/works/OL15413532W", "authors": [{"author": {"key": "/authors/OL29772A"}, "type": {"key": "/type/author_role"}}], "subject_times": ["332-30 B.C."], "type": {"key": "/type/work"}, "excerpts": [{"pages": "1", "excerpt": "Among the most famous women to have lived, Cleopatra VII ruled Egypt for twenty-two years.", "comment": "First line.", "author": {"key": "/people/sklibrarian"}}], "links": [{"title": "New York Times review", "url": "http://www.nytimes.com/2010/11/07/books/review/Harrison-t.html", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "New York Times review", "url": "http://www.nytimes.com/2010/11/02/books/02book.html", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}], "latest_revision": 13, "revision": 13, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2010-10-21T18:06:41.225510"}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2023-12-21T20:18:22.356652"}}